{"title": "A reduced cardiac reaction--diffusion wave", "pages": [{"page": 1, "frame": 1, "title": "A reduced cardiac reaction--diffusion wave", "step": 1, "steps": 1, "src": "deck/page-0001.svg", "text": "Computational Cardiology Lecture 10\nA reduced cardiac reaction–diﬀusion wave\nZan Ahmad\nFall 2024"}, {"page": 2, "frame": 2, "title": "A scaled cardiac reaction system", "step": 1, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0002.svg", "text": "A scaled cardiac reaction system\nvt = hv2(1 − v)τin − vτout + I + Dvxx.\nv, h are dimensionless; time is ms and distance is cm.\nComputational Cardiology Notes 2 / 20"}, {"page": 3, "frame": 2, "title": "A scaled cardiac reaction system", "step": 2, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0003.svg", "text": "A scaled cardiac reaction system\nvt = hv2(1 − v)τin − vτout + I + Dvxx.\nv, h are dimensionless; time is ms and distance is cm.\nComputational Cardiology Notes 2 / 20"}, {"page": 4, "frame": 3, "title": "The recovery gate", "step": 1, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0004.svg", "text": "The recovery gate\nht =\n{\n(1 − h)/τopen, v < v gate,\n−h/τclose, v ≥ vgate.\nEquality uses the closing branch.\nComputational Cardiology Notes 3 / 20"}, {"page": 5, "frame": 3, "title": "The recovery gate", "step": 2, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0005.svg", "text": "The recovery gate\nht =\n{\n(1 − h)/τopen, v < v gate,\n−h/τclose, v ≥ vgate.\nEquality uses the closing branch.\nComputational Cardiology Notes 3 / 20"}, {"page": 6, "frame": 4, "title": "The resting state", "step": 1, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0006.svg", "text": "The resting state\n(v, h) = (0 , 1), I = 0.\nBoth local derivatives vanish. Homogeneous diﬀusion also vanishes.\nComputational Cardiology Notes 4 / 20"}, {"page": 7, "frame": 4, "title": "The resting state", "step": 2, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0007.svg", "text": "The resting state\n(v, h) = (0 , 1), I = 0.\nBoth local derivatives vanish. Homogeneous diﬀusion also vanishes.\nComputational Cardiology Notes 4 / 20"}, {"page": 8, "frame": 5, "title": "Shared diffusive face fluxes", "step": 1, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0008.svg", "text": "Shared diﬀusive face ﬂuxes\nFi+1/2 = −D vi+1 − vi∆x , ˙vi = Fi−1/2 − Fi+1/2∆x .\nSealed endpoints have zero face ﬂux.\nComputational Cardiology Notes 5 / 20"}, {"page": 9, "frame": 5, "title": "Shared diffusive face fluxes", "step": 2, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0009.svg", "text": "Shared diﬀusive face ﬂuxes\nFi+1/2 = −D vi+1 − vi∆x , ˙vi = Fi−1/2 − Fi+1/2∆x .\nSealed endpoints have zero face ﬂux.\nComputational Cardiology Notes 5 / 20"}, {"page": 10, "frame": 6, "title": "The chain Laplacian", "step": 1, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0010.svg", "text": "The chain Laplacian\n˙v = −Lhv, L h1 = 0.\nvTLhv = D∆x2 ∑i (vi+1 − vi)2 ≥ 0.\nComputational Cardiology Notes 6 / 20"}, {"page": 11, "frame": 6, "title": "The chain Laplacian", "step": 2, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0011.svg", "text": "The chain Laplacian\n˙v = −Lhv, L h1 = 0.\nvTLhv = D∆x2 ∑i (vi+1 − vi)2 ≥ 0.\nComputational Cardiology Notes 6 / 20"}, {"page": 12, "frame": 7, "title": "Exact frozen-branch gate evolution", "step": 1, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0012.svg", "text": "Exact frozen-branch gate evolution\nBelow threshold, h∗ = 1 + ( hn − 1)e−∆t/τopen.\nAbove threshold, h∗ = hne−∆t/τclose. Both\npreserve [0, 1].\nComputational Cardiology Notes 7 / 20"}, {"page": 13, "frame": 7, "title": "Exact frozen-branch gate evolution", "step": 2, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0013.svg", "text": "Exact frozen-branch gate evolution\nBelow threshold, h∗ = 1 + ( hn − 1)e−∆t/τopen. Above threshold, h∗ = hne−∆t/τclose. Both\npreserve [0, 1].\nComputational Cardiology Notes 7 / 20"}, {"page": 14, "frame": 8, "title": "A semi-implicit reaction step", "step": 1, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0014.svg", "text": "A semi-implicit reaction step\na = h∗(vn)2\nτin\n, v ∗ = vn + ∆t(a + I)1 + ∆t(a + 1/τout) .\nActivation is frozen while the remaining linear factors are implicit.\nComputational Cardiology Notes 8 / 20"}, {"page": 15, "frame": 8, "title": "A semi-implicit reaction step", "step": 2, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0015.svg", "text": "A semi-implicit reaction step\na = h∗(vn)2\nτin\n, v ∗ = vn + ∆t(a + I)1 + ∆t(a + 1/τout) .\nActivation is frozen while the remaining linear factors are implicit.\nComputational Cardiology Notes 8 / 20"}, {"page": 16, "frame": 9, "title": "Prove the upper bound", "step": 1, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0016.svg", "text": "Prove the upper bound\ndenominator − numerator = 1 − vn + ∆t(1/τout − I).\nIt is nonnegative if vn ≤ 1 and I ≤ 1/τout.\nComputational Cardiology Notes 9 / 20"}, {"page": 17, "frame": 9, "title": "Prove the upper bound", "step": 2, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0017.svg", "text": "Prove the upper bound\ndenominator − numerator = 1 − vn + ∆t(1/τout − I).\nIt is nonnegative if vn ≤ 1 and I ≤ 1/τout.\nComputational Cardiology Notes 9 / 20"}, {"page": 18, "frame": 10, "title": "Implicit diffusion preserves the range", "step": 1, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0018.svg", "text": "Implicit diﬀusion preserves the range\n(I + ∆tLh)vn+1 = v∗.\nThe inverse is nonnegative and preserves constants, so it maps bounded data into the\nsame interval.\nComputational Cardiology Notes 10 / 20"}, {"page": 19, "frame": 10, "title": "Implicit diffusion preserves the range", "step": 2, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0019.svg", "text": "Implicit diﬀusion preserves the range\n(I + ∆tLh)vn+1 = v∗.\nThe inverse is nonnegative and preserves constants, so it maps bounded data into the\nsame interval.\nComputational Cardiology Notes 10 / 20"}, {"page": 20, "frame": 11, "title": "Reduced cardiac front", "step": 1, "steps": 1, "src": "deck/page-0020.svg", "text": "Reduced cardiac front\n0 5 10 15 20\nPosition along strand (mm)\n0.00\n0.25\n0.50\n0.75Scaled cardiac voltage v\n10 ms\n20 ms\n30 ms\n40 ms\nComputational Cardiology Notes 11 / 20"}, {"page": 21, "frame": 12, "title": "Two physical sensors", "step": 1, "steps": 1, "src": "deck/page-0021.svg", "text": "Two physical sensors\n0 20 40 60 80\nTime (ms)\n0.00\n0.25\n0.50\n0.75Scaled cardiac voltage v\nx=6 mm x=12 mm\nComputational Cardiology Notes 12 / 20"}, {"page": 22, "frame": 13, "title": "A fixed spatial source", "step": 1, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0022.svg", "text": "A ﬁxed spatial source\nIi = I0\n|Ki ∩ [0, ℓs]|\n∆x .\nFractional overlap preserves the source width under mesh reﬁnement.\nComputational Cardiology Notes 13 / 20"}, {"page": 23, "frame": 13, "title": "A fixed spatial source", "step": 2, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0023.svg", "text": "A ﬁxed spatial source\nIi = I0\n|Ki ∩ [0, ℓs]|\n∆x .\nFractional overlap preserves the source width under mesh reﬁnement.\nComputational Cardiology Notes 13 / 20"}, {"page": 24, "frame": 14, "title": "A fixed temporal source", "step": 1, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0024.svg", "text": "A ﬁxed temporal source\n∫ ∫\nI dx dt = I0ℓsTs = .02 cm .\nThese are scaled-voltage integral units, not microcoulombs.\nComputational Cardiology Notes 14 / 20"}, {"page": 25, "frame": 14, "title": "A fixed temporal source", "step": 2, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0025.svg", "text": "A ﬁxed temporal source\n∫ ∫\nI dx dt = I0ℓsTs = .02 cm .\nThese are scaled-voltage integral units, not microcoulombs.\nComputational Cardiology Notes 14 / 20"}, {"page": 26, "frame": 15, "title": "Interpolate an upward crossing", "step": 1, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0026.svg", "text": "Interpolate an upward crossing\nt∗ = t0 + v∗ − v0v1 − v0 (t1 − t0).\nA valid upward bracket and unequal endpoint values are required.\nComputational Cardiology Notes 15 / 20"}, {"page": 27, "frame": 15, "title": "Interpolate an upward crossing", "step": 2, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0027.svg", "text": "Interpolate an upward crossing\nt∗ = t0 + v∗ − v0v1 − v0 (t1 − t0).\nA valid upward bracket and unequal endpoint values are required.\nComputational Cardiology Notes 15 / 20"}, {"page": 28, "frame": 16, "title": "Define the measured speed", "step": 1, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0028.svg", "text": "Deﬁne the measured speed\nc = x2 − x1\nt∗,2 − t∗,1\n.\nSensors at .6 and 1.2 cm use the same v∗ = .5 criterion.\nComputational Cardiology Notes 16 / 20"}, {"page": 29, "frame": 16, "title": "Define the measured speed", "step": 2, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0029.svg", "text": "Deﬁne the measured speed\nc = x2 − x1\nt∗,2 − t∗,1\n.\nSensors at .6 and 1.2 cm use the same v∗ = .5 criterion.\nComputational Cardiology Notes 16 / 20"}, {"page": 30, "frame": 17, "title": "Refine space", "step": 1, "steps": 1, "src": "deck/page-0030.svg", "text": "Reﬁne space\n100 200 400\nCell count (dt = 0.01 ms)\n0.3370\n0.3375\n0.3380\n0.3385\n0.3390Measured speed (m/s)\nComputational Cardiology Notes 17 / 20"}, {"page": 31, "frame": 18, "title": "Refine time", "step": 1, "steps": 1, "src": "deck/page-0031.svg", "text": "Reﬁne time\n0.01 0.04 0.08\nTime step (ms; 400 cells)\n0.325\n0.330\n0.335Measured speed (m/s)\nComputational Cardiology Notes 18 / 20"}, {"page": 32, "frame": 19, "title": "Timing error propagates into speed", "step": 1, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0032.svg", "text": "Timing error propagates into speed\nδc\nc ≃ − δ∆ts∆ts\nfor ﬁxed sensor separation.\nSpatial and temporal reﬁnement must retain the same stimulus\nand sensor deﬁnitions.\nComputational Cardiology Notes 19 / 20"}, {"page": 33, "frame": 19, "title": "Timing error propagates into speed", "step": 2, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0033.svg", "text": "Timing error propagates into speed\nδc\nc ≃ − δ∆ts∆ts\nfor ﬁxed sensor separation. Spatial and temporal reﬁnement must retain the same stimulus\nand sensor deﬁnitions.\nComputational Cardiology Notes 19 / 20"}, {"page": 34, "frame": 20, "title": "Scope of the propagation result", "step": 1, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0034.svg", "text": "Scope of the propagation result\nThe homogeneous sealed strand omits anisotropy, branching and extracellular potential.\nBounded states and a plausible speed do not establish a tissue-speciﬁc physiological\ncalibration.\nComputational Cardiology Notes 20 / 20"}, {"page": 35, "frame": 20, "title": "Scope of the propagation result", "step": 2, "steps": 2, "src": "deck/page-0035.svg", "text": "Scope of the propagation result\nThe homogeneous sealed strand omits anisotropy, branching and extracellular potential.\nBounded states and a plausible speed do not establish a tissue-speciﬁc physiological\ncalibration.\nComputational Cardiology Notes 20 / 20"}], "frames": [{"frame": 1, "title": "A reduced cardiac reaction--diffusion wave", "start": 0, "end": 0, "id": "title", "notes": {"id": "the-scaled-cardiac-reaction-system", "title": "The scaled cardiac reaction system", "page": 1, "destination": "note-the-scaled-cardiac-reaction-system", "href": "notes.pdf#page=1"}, "modules": []}, {"frame": 2, "title": "A scaled cardiac reaction system", "start": 1, "end": 2, "id": "a-scaled-cardiac-reaction-system", "notes": {"id": "the-scaled-cardiac-reaction-system", "title": "The scaled cardiac reaction system", "page": 1, "destination": "note-the-scaled-cardiac-reaction-system", "href": "notes.pdf#page=1"}, "modules": [{"id": "excitable-wave", "title": "Excitation and propagation", "href": "../modules/animations/excitable-wave.html", "notes_sections": ["the-scaled-cardiac-reaction-system", "conservative-coupling-on-a-sealed-strand", "gate-reaction-and-diffusion-substeps", "a-fixed-physical-stimulus-and-sensor-geometry", "threshold-arrival-and-conduction-speed", "component-analysis-and-coupled-refinement"], "slide_ids": ["a-scaled-cardiac-reaction-system", "the-recovery-gate", "the-resting-state", "shared-diffusive-face-fluxes", "the-chain-laplacian", "exact-frozen-branch-gate-evolution", "a-semi-implicit-reaction-step", "prove-the-upper-bound", "implicit-diffusion-preserves-the-range", "a-fixed-spatial-source", "a-fixed-temporal-source", "interpolate-an-upward-crossing", "define-the-measured-speed", "timing-error-propagates-into-speed", "scope-of-the-propagation-